# Per-machine IDE state. These record which emulator you last ran on, how you
# sorted the device list, and what your local JDK happens to be called, so they
# churn on every machine and show up in the commit dialog forever.
# deploymentTargetSelector.xml was still carrying one teammate's macOS avd path;
# misc.xml flips between "temurin-25" and "25" depending on whose install it is.
#
# misc.xml also holds languageLevel, which looks shared but isn't authoritative:
# Gradle's compileOptions is what actually compiles the code, and the IDE
# rewrites this file from Gradle on every sync.
#
# The rest of Vinyl/.idea/ stays tracked on purpose: codeStyles, inspection
# profiles and run configurations are genuinely shared settings.
/.idea/deploymentTargetSelector.xml
/.idea/deviceManager.xml
/.idea/misc.xml
.DS_Store
/build
/captures
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
local.properties
